-- GENERATED by scripts/census/gen_time_views.py -- do not hand-edit.
--
-- THE SHARED TIMELINE. Every clocked table in the warehouse on one
-- axis, at one row per (source, clock kind, grain, day).
--
-- What it answers that nothing else could:
--   * what was happening ANYWHERE in the warehouse in a given month
--   * which sources go quiet, and exactly when
--   * which sources cover a date at all, before a question is asked
--   * how many independent sources touch the same day
--
-- What it is NOT: row detail. It counts. Open the matching view in
-- LIBRARY_MARTS.TIMELINE for the rows behind a count.
--
-- ALWAYS respect ripple_grain. A year-grain source contributes a single
-- stack on Jan 1; treating that as a daily event invents a spike.
-- ALWAYS respect ripple_clock. Summing a 'happened' source and a
-- 'reported' source into one line mixes two different questions.
--
-- WHY A VIEW (2026-08-31): the domain index rollups are TABLES, so the
-- planned/actual tag they store is frozen at build time and goes stale
-- the moment a 'planned' date passes. This view re-derives the tag at
-- read time against current_date, using the registry's base clock kind
-- for the source. The rollups stay cheap; the label stays honest.

